LICENSING
---------

Mesh is distributed under the MIT License (see LICENSE). Per Apache 2.0
Section 4, the following modifications have been made relative to the
upstream code:

  1. Removed six direct API providers (Gemini, OpenAI, Azure, X.AI, DIAL,
     Custom) and the corresponding catalogue JSONs, environment variables,
     and tests.
  2. Renamed the project from "pal" / "PAL MCP Server" to "Mesh MCP Server".
  3. Rewrote the CLI provider implementations (providers/gemini_cli.py and
     providers/codex_cli.py) to invoke the real `gemini -p ... -o json` and
     `codex exec --json` shapes (the upstream invented schemas did not match
     the actual CLI binaries).
  4. Replaced ~12,000 lines of provider code, marketing copy, and dead
     scripts with a focused CLI-first implementation.
  5. Reset the licence to MIT for simpler downstream consumption. Inherited
     code is small enough that this is intended as relicensing of the
     derivative work, not the upstream itself; the upstream's Apache 2.0
     terms remain in force for anyone using the upstream directly.

